    <string name="formation_desc_433">Attacking with width. Three forwards create constant threat.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_442">Classic balance: two strikers and two banks of four.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_4231">A double pivot shields the back four behind a creative trio.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_451">Crowd the midfield, win the ball and break with one striker.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_343">Three at the back and a front three that never stops pressing.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_352">Wing-backs give the width while two strikers stay central.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_541">Five defenders and four midfielders. Hard to break down.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_41212">The narrow diamond: a holder, two runners and a No. 10 behind two strikers.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_4411">A second striker drops in to link midfield and attack.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_532">A solid back five with two strikers up top.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_3412">Wing-backs stretch the pitch while a No. 10 feeds two strikers.</string>
    <string name="formation_desc_4222">Two holders, two inside forwards and two strikers in a box.</string>

